    "text": "By Grace Koennecke ,\n7 hours ago PUTNAM COUNTY, W.Va. (WSAZ) - West Virginia Governor Patrick Morrisey announced a $25 million, 100,000 square foot manufacturing facility will be built in the state. The governor says the facility will be in Putnam County. The governor’s office says it’s part of a $25 million investment from global engineering group... Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 2",
